# Fork-owned CI files: never take upstream's version when merging
# E4-Computer-Engineering/nvme-exporter into this fork. These files diverge
# on purpose (floating action majors, multi-arch docker publishing) and
# Renovate keeps them current, so upstream's edits are deliberately dropped.
# Dockerfile and Makefile are NOT listed: their upstream changes are
# functional, so conflicts there must surface and fail the sync loudly.
#
# The "ours" merge driver is NOT builtin - it only works where
# `git config merge.ours.driver true` has been set. The upstream-sync workflow
# sets it; if you run the merge locally, set it in your clone too or these
# attributes are inert and you get normal conflicts.
.github/workflows/build.yml merge=ours
.github/workflows/docker.yml merge=ours
.github/workflows/release.yml merge=ours
.github/workflows/upstream-sync.yaml merge=ours
renovate.json merge=ours
